 "what_is_drawn": "arm C is the v1.49.2 CANDIDATE STAGE, not the mask the application emits. detect_one.py runs unified_pipeline.run_unified_pipeline, which adds PASS 2 (concavity, bridge-corridor, interior-fill) and with the classifier off keeps every Pass-2 row too, so the app's mask is a superset of every arm-C mask here. Pass 2 is defined on a whole micrograph resolved from ORIGINAL_DIR, not on a 512 px crop.",
 "arms": {
  "v147": "A: single flattening radius sigma=40, logistic region classifier at threshold 0.5538 (analysis/research/crackpipe.py)",
  "ablation": "B: arm A's candidate stage with the classifier bypassed, every region kept. One variable differs from A. This is the arm whose numbers analysis/detector_overrides.py publishes.",
  "v1492": "C: the v1.49.2 CANDIDATE STAGE -- darkness cut unioned over flattening radii (5,10,20,40,80,160,320) at mad_k 5.0, background for sigma>64 estimated on a decimated copy, cleaned, and stopping there. Bound out of detector_overrides.install() by analysis/research/improve/angle4_shipped.py. This was the whole emission while USE_REGION_CLASSIFIER was False except for the area floor, which arm D adds.",
  "v1492_floor": "D: arm C with the 40 px component floor the application applies, classifier still bypassed. C -> D is the floor's own effect.",
  "shipped_lofo": "F: arm E with every tile scored out of sample. For the 9 tiles whose parent micrograph is in the bundle's training image list the classifier is refitted without that micrograph's rows, by the same recipe (sem_classifier_lofo.fit); the other 17 are already out of sample and are unchanged. E -> F is the leakage, and nothing else.",
  "shipped": "E: arm D with the region classifier ON, which is what the application emits today. D -> E is the classifier's own effect, one variable, and it is the comparison every classifier claim in the paper rests on. Both arms call both_modalities.emit, so neither is a transcription."
